  "details": "The \"Change Clock Settings\" feature offers incredibly detailed configuration options and excellent customizability, which is fantastic—but there’s still one thing missing.\n\nThat is the “30-hour format” commonly used in Japan.\n\nIt’s an extension of the 24-hour format, where times past midnight are expressed as a continuation of the previous day. For example, 1:00 AM the next day would be displayed as 25:00 today, and 5:59 AM the next day would be shown as 29:59 today.\n\nThis 30-hour format is often used for late-night TV programs in Japan. It aligns perfectly with platforms like VRChat, which have a high number of late-night users.\n\nThis request is not a joke, but a practicality. It is actually used in the Japanese broadcasting industry, railroad industry, and astronomical observation.",
